# Emulator disk images and installer media.
#
# These are build/runtime artifacts, not source: win95_extra_files.iso is
# ~1.2 GB and each win95_*.img is ~100 MB. GitHub rejects any single file over
# 100 MB outright, and a large blob that does get in stays in history forever
# even if it is deleted later -- so they are kept out deliberately rather than
# by oversight. Fetch or rebuild them locally.
*.img
*.iso
*.img.zst
*.zst

# ...except the two drives win95all.ini boots, shipped COMPRESSED. main.js
# decompresses *.img.zst in the browser (see unzstdBytes), so the raw .img
# files are not needed in the repo at all: 42.6 + 42.9 MB instead of 90 + 95,
# and both sit under GitHub's 50 MB warning threshold rather than over it.
#
# Compressed with an 8 MiB window on purpose. unzstd.wasm allocates the
# frame's window at decode time in the browser, and a default --ultra -22
# window of 128 MiB may fail there -- which presents as a corrupt disk image,
# not as a compression setting. Keep wlog at 23 when recompressing.
!win95_c_drive.img.zst
!win95_d_drive_all.img.zst

# The wasm and firmware blobs are REQUIRED AT RUNTIME, not optional build
# output: index.html fetches tiny386.wasm, unzstd.wasm, bios.bin and vgabios.bin
# on every boot. Ignoring them made a fresh clone fail immediately -- the fetch
# 404s, the HTML error page comes back instead, and the browser reports
#     CompileError: expected magic word 00 61 73 6d, found 3c 21 44 4f
# ("<!DO", i.e. the 404 page). They total ~590 KB, so there is no reason not to
# ship them.

# Timestamped safety copies made while editing.
.backup-*/

.codex/
.agents/
Examples/
